## Impact
This vulnerability can lead to cross-site scripting (XSS) on websites that include Webpack-generated files and allow users to inject certain scriptless HTML tags with improperly sanitized name or id attributes.

## Patch
A possible patch to this vulnerability could refer to the Google Closure project which makes itself resistant to DOM Clobbering attack: [google/closure-library@b312823/closure/goog/base.js#L174](https://github.com/google/closure-library/blob/b312823ec5f84239ff1db7526f4a75cba0420a33/closure/goog/base.js#L174)
